{
  "dom_id": "step-q90453",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[6X+2].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}},\\,x\\ge 1\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[6X+2]=6\\text{E}[X]+2\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }x\\cdot \\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={-\\frac{4}{3{x}^{3}}|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[6X+2] & =6\\text{E}[X]+2 \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}+2 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
